# Final Release Flow

```text
Developer Commit
   ↓
Backend / Frontend / Agent / Data Science / Data Engineering Pipeline Trigger
   ↓
Build + Unit Tests + Lint + Contract Validation
   ↓
Deploy to Dev
   ↓
Dev Smoke Testing
   ↓
Deploy to QA
   ↓
QA Functional + Regression + Data Validation
   ↓
QA Signoff
   ↓
Production Approval Gate
   ↓
Deploy to Production
   ↓
Production Smoke Test
   ↓
Monitoring + Alerts + Release Notes
```

This gives you a clean ADO structure with **23 consolidated features**, each broken into **stories and implementation tickets**.
